{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:88262",
  "title": "Important: buildah security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-23 12:11:02"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-24 00:12:29"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The buildah package provides a tool for facilitating building OCI container images. Among other things, buildah enables you to: Create a working container, either from scratch or using an image as a starting point; Create an image, either from a working container or using the instructions in a Dockerfile; Build both Docker and OCI images. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* podman: Arbitrary file write when importing OCI archive (CVE-2025-11395)\n\n* net/http: golang: golang: Denial of Service via crafted HTTP Range headers (CVE-2026-78667)\n\n* net/http: net/http/internal/http2: golang.org/x/net/http2: net/http: Denial of Service via excessive HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames (CVE-2026-78669)\n\n* crypto/x509: golang: crypto/x509: Man-in-the-middle attacks via untrusted intermediate certificates (CVE-2026-111943)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
